{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## DESIGN + PROOF — causal-stability history reclamation as the tickets-branch pack-shrink lever (NO prod mutation; escalation, not execution)\n\nContext: health-lane bug `defensive-buckskin-rhino` (`a453-193b-2864-451b`) — the blobless CI checkout pack is ~481 MiB vs the deliberate 100 MiB budget (`verify-identity.yml:47`). This design proves the causal-stability boundary 536b owns, quantifies the achievable pack shrink, designs the safe mechanism, and states the risk/rollback. **No history rewrite / force-push / destructive reclaim was performed.**\n\n### Measured evidence (origin/tickets @ 2026-08-29; local dev object store is bloated/garbage-packed so ratios, not its absolute on-disk, are load-bearing)\n- Commits: **235,482** on `tickets` vs 2,880 on `main`. History age: 2026-06-08 → now (~82 days).\n- Blobless reachable object composition (`rev-list --objects --filter=blob:none | cat-file --batch-check`): **235,482 commits** (inflated 62.4 MiB) + **408,295 trees** (inflated 42.7 GiB) + **ZERO blobs**. Trees ≈ **95%** of blobless bytes → matches the bug's \"~90% trees / ~10% commits / zero blobs\" and ~428K trees.\n- Root tree = **270 KB, 6,008 entries** (one flat dir per ticket), **re-emitted on every commit** → ~235K near-identical 270 KB root trees is the tree whale.\n- Fresh CI repack = 481 MiB ⇒ **~2.0 KiB/commit** on-disk (blobless).\n- Commit-type mix (40K sample): enrichment quartet ENQUEUE/CLAIM/DONE_ENRICH ≈ **52%** + TICKET_DIGEST ≈ **17%** + Merge ≈ 21% (overlapping). Semantic user ops (CREATE/EDIT/COMMENT/STATUS/LINK/CLAIM…) are a small minority. Merges total 38,041 (16%). ⇒ **~69% of history is derived enrichment/digest churn.**\n- Commit age: last **7d = 100,072**; **30d = 183,777**; 60d = 222,838; all ≈ 235,482. Write rate ≈ **14K commits/day**.\n\n### The causal-stability boundary (proof)\nCitations: I1 (concurrency.md §\"The invariants\", `*.retired` lifecycle \"safe only past causal stability\"); I9 (compaction safe vs concurrent remote appends — \"never retire an event whose content a not-yet-folded state could still need\"); I9b (compaction runs out-of-band in its own clone); sync reconverges by **MERGE-as-union, never rebase** (bug 637b); operator decision on this ticket (2026-08-24: **option 2 remote-anchored horizon + stale-clone forced override**, N=30d, residual >N-day loss ACCEPTED); authorship: SNAPSHOT `authorship_ledger` = per signed folded event `{event_uuid, content_hash, signature, signer_pubkey, position(ts-uuid + introducing commit_sha)}` (`compact_txn._build_authorship_ledger`); era rule is commit-ancestry (`attest/authorship.py` `verify_authorship_at_commit`); grandfather anchor `identity.enforce_since` (`rebar.toml:143`); `require_authenticated=false` today (signature lane advisory; the **pack-size guard fails closed unconditionally**).\n\n**Theorem.** An event E in ticket T is safe to reclaim from `tickets` history (drop its per-event commit + trees; remove/retire its file) IFF all of:\n- **C1 (folded):** E is folded by a committed SNAPSHOT S of T (E is `.retired` under S); E's still-observable contribution is fully captured in S.compiled_state. [I1]\n- **C2 (remote-aged):** S's folding compaction commit has been reachable from the sync remote's `tickets` ref for ≥ N days. Every clone that pushes/pulls converges through the remote, so within N days every *live* clone has observed the fold. [operator decision]\n- **C3 (override):** the stale-clone-override invariant holds — any clone whose last remote convergence is older than N days is **forced to reset local `tickets` to remote** on reconnect and may NOT reintroduce E by merge/rebase. This converts \"no clone *should* be partitioned > N days\" from probabilistic to **enforced**, closing the I1 resurrection hole. [operator decision]\n- **C4 (verifiability):** E's signed record is carried in S.authorship_ledger with a resolvable era check, **OR** `identity.enforce_since` is re-anchored to the reclamation baseline so E is grandfathered (reported, never fails). [gnu-whale-ichor; enforce_since]\n- **C5 (no unfolded dependence):** no not-yet-folded event needs E's content — satisfied because S folds E and every later event post-dates S. [I9]\n\nUnder C1–C5, reclaiming E changes **no still-observable ticket state** (reads reduce from S), breaks **no** signature verification (C4), and **cannot be resurrected** (C2+C3: no live clone holds E active; stale clones are overridden), and cannot violate optimistic-concurrency/audit (the audit trail's signed content is preserved in the ledger + backup ref).\n\n**Safe to reclaim below the boundary:** `.retired` tombstones folded by a horizon-aged SNAPSHOT; superseded TICKET_DIGEST events (only the latest digest is observable); enrichment-quartet intermediates (ENQUEUE/CLAIM_ENRICH) whose terminal DONE_ENRICH is folded; redundant auto-reconcile MERGE commits with no unique tree delta below the horizon; **and the per-event COMMITS + root/dir TREES of all events folded into a horizon-aged SNAPSHOT — collapsed into ONE checkpoint** (the object-count reducer).\n**NOT safe:** anything inside the horizon (< N days remote-reachable — an in-flight clone may still merge it); forward-compat unknown-type events (compact partitions them out, never absorbs); the latest SNAPSHOT per ticket + any live post-SNAPSHOT events; any post-`enforce_since` event whose authorship_ledger record can't be reconstructed unless enforce_since is re-anchored; CREATE genesis carrying `creation_channel` unless folded into compiled_state or retained (I9a).\n\n### Quantified win vs the 100 MiB budget — **it does NOT get under budget alone**\n1. **`.retired` GC alone (536b's literal scope) shrinks the blobless pack by ~0.** `.retired` files are BLOBS; the CI-guarded pack is BLOBLESS (zero blobs). Removing blobs from a blobless pack is a no-op; done as a *forward* delete it ADDS commits/trees (net worse). The literal ticket scope cannot move this gate.\n2. **The only lever is reducing reachable COMMIT + TREE count** ⇒ collapse the per-event history into SNAPSHOT-anchored checkpoints below the horizon (a history rewrite), re-signed/re-anchored.\n3. Max safe win: **N=30d** → 51,705 pre-horizon commits collapse to ~1 checkpoint (+~6,008 baseline dir trees); surviving ≈ 183,777 recent commits × ~2.0 KiB ≈ **~365–380 MiB** (~24% off). **N=7d** → ≈100,072 commits ≈ **~200–215 MiB**. To reach ≤100 MiB needs ≤ ~48K surviving commits ⇒ horizon **< ~4 days** — unsafe (operator accepted 30d, not 4d; a 4-day-offline clone would be force-overridden).\n   ⇒ **Causal-stability coalescing at ANY safe horizon cannot get the blobless pack under 100 MiB.** Root cause is write→commit amplification (~14K commits/day, ~69% derived churn, each re-emitting a 270 KB / 6,008-entry root tree). History GC is symptomatic; the disease is per-event commit granularity + full-width root-tree churn. At ~28 MiB/day growth, even a rewrite to 365 MiB re-crosses 481 MiB in ~4 days.\n\n**Therefore a temporary budget-raise BRIDGE is unavoidable**, paired with two structural fixes that are OUT of 536b's scope (new tickets, `discovered_from` this epic):\n- **W1 — write-amplification reduction:** batch the enrichment + digest lane so it is not one-commit-per-event on the shared branch (ADR 0039 already batches commits import-only; extend to the enrichment/digest writers). Biggest durable lever.\n- **W2 — root-tree width reduction:** shard the 6,008 flat ticket dirs into a fan-out (e.g. `ab/abcd-…`) so each commit re-emits a small subtree, not a 270 KB root tree — cuts tree bytes/commit ~50–100×.\n- **W3 — budget bridge:** deliberately raise `REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB` (e.g. ~600 MiB) with a documented re-evaluation date, so the health lane is GREEN while coalescing + W1 + W2 land. Only way to green the gate on the near horizon without an unsafe sub-4-day rewrite.\n\n### Mechanism (safe, portable, repeatable — DESIGN only)\nOffline, out-of-band, in a **disposable clone on a separate machine** (mirrors I9b compact-sweep isolation; re-derives from `origin/tickets`; never on an interactive path; never holds the store lock). Portable per `project.portability`: pure git reachability + commit timestamps + in-process reduce — no single-CI-provider trigger; invokable by library/CLI (`rebar compact-gc` / `compact --reclaim`) in any environment or none.\n- **P1 eligibility (536b S1):** per ticket find the horizon-aged SNAPSHOT (folding commit reachable on `origin/tickets` ≥ N days).\n- **P2 coalesce (536b S2, escalated to commit/tree reclamation):** build a NEW baseline root commit = the compacted as-of-horizon state (one checkpoint tree per ticket = its SNAPSHOT compiled_state + live events + carried `authorship_ledger`), then replay in-horizon commits on top. Re-sign the baseline; **re-anchor `identity.enforce_since` to the baseline commit** so all pre-baseline events are grandfathered (already verified pre-rewrite, captured in the ledger). The SNAPSHOT is what makes this sound — compaction already proved the pre-SNAPSHOT log redundant for reads.\n- **S3 stale-clone override:** live clones (< N days) merge normally at swap; staler clones are refused a reintroducing merge and reset to remote (accepted loss).\n\n### Interaction with the auto-push remote + worktrees, risk, rollback\nThe `tickets` branch auto-commits+auto-pushes on every write. A history rewrite changes every commit SHA ⇒ **every consumer's local `tickets` and every tracking worktree diverges (no common ancestor)** — a non-FF force-update of a shared, ~14K-writes/day branch. Sharp edge: a **live** clone with UNPUSHED in-flight writes at swap time loses them unless the swap **fences writes** (quiesce the remote, drain pushes, swap) — so P2 needs a maintenance window, non-trivial for a continuously-pushing store.\n- **Failure modes:** (a) lost unpushed writes during the swap; (b) a never-fetching clone keeps old history and could clobber on a later push (mitigate: remote non-FF protection + override); (c) wrong `enforce_since` re-anchor → post-baseline events fail the merge-gate; (d) fsck/replay breakage if a needed `.retired`/CREATE genesis was dropped without folding (I9a `creation_channel`).\n- **Rollback:** (1) pin immutable backup ref `refs/tickets-backup/pre-reclaim-<date>` to the old tip BEFORE the swap, retain ≥ 2×N days; (2) stage on a shadow remote/branch first, verified with `rebar fsck` + full-log replay + `rebar verify-authorship` before promoting; (3) the swap is one ref update, revertible to the backup ref within the window; (4) never prune the backup pack until a green Verify Authorship Identity run + a full reconcile cycle confirm health.\n\n### Recommendation (escalated for human approval — HARD STOP here)\n1. Adopt the C1–C5 boundary as the shared safety envelope (sound; matches the operator decision).\n2. 536b's literal `.retired` GC does **not** unblock the health lane; **broaden the epic's reclamation target to COMMIT/TREE history coalescing** (the object-count lever), with `.retired`/digest/enrichment reclamation being the content the coalescing drops.\n3. **A temporary budget-raise bridge (W3) is unavoidable** to green the gate now, because even maximal safe coalescing lands ~365 MiB; pair it with structural fixes W1 (write-batching) + W2 (root-tree sharding) as the durable path.\n4. **Do not execute the rewrite/force-push without human approval** — high blast radius on a shared, auto-pushed, event-sourced branch. This slice ends at PLAN + PROOF.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788034827271416403,"uuid":"16760c1b-da7c-4753-a2a1-8c52e2863c28"}